Here is an OWL ontology design pattern (ODP) in Turtle syntax that addresses the scenario and competency questions:
```turtle
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>.
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>.
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>.
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>.
@prefix :     <http://example.org/odp#>.

:Ontology a owl:Ontology ;
rdfs:label "Temporal Indirection Ontology" ;
rdfs:comment "An ontology for modeling temporal indirection in various domains.".

; Scenario-requirement-to-axiom mapping

; 1. Persistent identifier is a stable referent
:PersistentIdentifier a owl:Class ;
rdfs:label "Persistent Identifier" ;
rdfs:comment "A class representing a persistent identifier, which is a stable referent.".

; 2. Referent is a dynamic concept
:Referent a owl:Class ;
rdfs:label "Referent" ;
rdfs:comment "A class representing the referent of a persistent identifier, which can change over time.".

; 3. Temporal binding is a relationship between a persistent identifier and a referent
:TemporalBinding a owl:Class ;
rdfs:label "Temporal Binding" ;
rdfs:comment "A class representing the relationship between a persistent identifier and a referent, which binds the identifier to the referent at a specific time.".

; 4. Referent transition occurs when a persistent identifier references a new referent
:ReferentTransition a owl:Class ;
rdfs:label "Referent Transition" ;
rdfs:comment "A class representing a referent transition, which occurs when a persistent identifier references a new referent.".

; 5. Observations are associated with specific referents
:Observation a owl:Class ;
rdfs:label "Observation" ;
rdfs:comment "A class representing an observation, which is associated with a specific referent.".

; 6. Sequence of referents over time can be reconstructed
:ReferentSequence a owl:Class ;
rdfs:label "Referent Sequence" ;
rdfs:comment "A class representing a sequence of referents over time, which can be reconstructed from temporal bindings.".

; 7. Rules triggered specific transitions
:TransitionRule a owl:Class ;
rdfs:label "Transition Rule" ;
rdfs:comment "A class representing a rule that triggered a specific transition.".

; 8. Gaps or overlaps in temporal bindings can be detected
:TemporalGap a owl:Class ;
rdfs:label "Temporal Gap" ;
rdfs:comment "A class representing a gap in temporal bindings, which can be detected by comparing referent transitions.".

; 9. Complete context can be rebuilt for any time point
:RebuildContext a owl:Class ;
rdfs:label "Rebuild Context" ;
rdfs:comment "A class representing the ability to rebuild complete context for any time point, using temporal bindings and referent transitions.".

; CQ-to-axiom mapping

; 1. Which entity does a persistent identifier currently reference?
:CQ1 a owl:Class ;
rdfs:label "Current Referent" ;
rdfs:comment "A class representing the current referent of a persistent identifier.".

; 2. Which entity was referenced at a past timestamp?
:CQ2 a owl:Class ;
rdfs:label "Past Referent" ;
rdfs:comment "A class representing the referent of a persistent identifier at a past timestamp.".

; 3. When did referent transitions occur?
:CQ3 a owl:Class ;
rdfs:label "Transition Timestamps" ;
rdfs:comment "A class representing the timestamps of referent transitions.".

; 4